# ============================================================
# 🧠 CONCEPT: .dockerignore — not just a tidiness file
# WHY IT MATTERS (interview angle): everything in the build CONTEXT is
#   uploaded to the Docker daemon before the build starts. Leave
#   node_modules in and you ship hundreds of megabytes across that
#   boundary on every build, making even a cached build slow.
#   ⚠️ IT IS ALSO A SECURITY CONTROL: without it, `COPY . .` copies your
#   `.env` (real secrets) and `.git` (the entire history, including any
#   secret ever committed and later "removed") INTO THE IMAGE. Anyone who
#   can pull that image can read them. This is a real and frequent leak.
#   ⚠️ And a correctness one: a host node_modules built on Windows/macOS
#   contains platform-specific native binaries that will not run in a
#   Linux container.
# ============================================================

node_modules
npm-debug.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.git
.gitignore
coverage
tests
*.test.js
uploads/*
!uploads/.gitkeep
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
